{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"See how FirebladeECS revisions compare on a shared workload suite, and run the comparison yourself."}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/firebladeecs\/benchmarks"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"metadata":{"role":"article","modules":[{"name":"FirebladeECS"}],"roleHeading":"Article","title":"Benchmarks"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS"]]},"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Overview","anchor":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The benchmark suite measures the same workloads at several committed FirebladeECS revisions, such as a release tag against ","type":"text"},{"code":"main","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". The workloads cover entity creation, destruction and lookup, adding and removing components, iterating families, system updates and component events. Revisions with value-type components run each workload on both the ","type":"text"},{"code":"archetype","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and the ","type":"text"},{"code":"sparseSet","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" storage (see ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/ChoosingAStorage","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":"), so a report also shows what the storage choice costs.","type":"text"}]},{"text":"How results are made trustworthy","type":"heading","level":3,"anchor":"How-results-are-made-trustworthy"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Each revision is built once and measured in ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"k"},{"type":"text","text":" independent process replicates, interleaved in a seeded random order. The replicate is the unit of analysis: the centre value is the median of the replicate medians, with a distribution-free order-statistic 95% confidence interval. A speed-up against the baseline is the Hodges–Lehmann estimate with its exact confidence interval, tested with an exact Mann–Whitney test and adjusted across all comparisons of a report with Benjamini–Hochberg. A change counts as "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"faster"},{"type":"text","text":" or "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"slower"},{"type":"text","text":" only when it is significant and clears the ±5% equivalence zone; an interval inside that zone is reported as "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"equivalent"},{"type":"text","text":", anything else as "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"inconclusive"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},{"text":"Read and reproduce","type":"heading","level":3,"anchor":"Read-and-reproduce"},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The latest published report: "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"https:\/\/fireblade-engine.github.io\/ecs\/benchmarks\/"},{"type":"text","text":". Reports are published for dedicated benchmark releases only; the page shows the newest."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The 2.0.0 report: "},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"https:\/\/fireblade-engine.github.io\/ecs\/benchmarks\/2.0.0\/","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":", the full suite with 10 replicates on both storages. Its source is committed as "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"https:\/\/github.com\/fireblade-engine\/ecs\/blob\/main\/Documentation\/Benchmarks\/BenchmarkReport.html"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The statistical design and workload parity notes: "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"https:\/\/github.com\/fireblade-engine\/ecs\/blob\/main\/Documentation\/Benchmarks\/Methodology.md"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"To measure revisions locally, pass comma-separated tags, branches or commit IDs. Results are saved under "},{"code":"Benchmarks\/Results\/<UTC timestamp>\/","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":":"}]},{"type":"codeListing","code":["make benchmark-compare REFS=1.4.3,main:2.0.0 REPLICATES=10 BENCHMARK_FILTER='.*'","make benchmark-report RESULTS=\"Benchmarks\/Results\/<run>\/*.json\" REPORT_BASELINE=1.4.3"],"syntax":"sh"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Without ","type":"text"},{"code":"BENCHMARK_FILTER","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" only 16 entities of every workload plus "},{"code":"entity.create.no-entities","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" (which only has 0 entities) run. "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"make benchmark-report"},{"type":"text","text":" renders the single file "},{"code":"BenchmarkReport.html","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" from saved results and never runs benchmarks. See "},{"code":"Benchmarks\/README.md","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" for all options."}]}],"kind":"content"}],"kind":"article","identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Benchmarks","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"seeAlsoSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/GettingStartedWithFirebladeECS","doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/ReadingAndWritingComponents","doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/ComponentMacro","doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/ReactingToNexusEvents","doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/ChoosingAStorage","doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/SavingAndLoadingScenes","doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/MigratingToFirebladeECS2","doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Nexus","doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/NexusEvent","doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/NexusEventDelegate","doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/NexusEventMask","doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Nexus\/StorageKind"],"generated":true,"anchor":"Essentials","title":"Essentials"}],"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"minor":3,"major":0},"sections":[],"references":{"doc://FirebladeECS/documentation/FirebladeECS/ReactingToNexusEvents":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Observe structural changes and, on request, changes of component values."}],"role":"article","kind":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/ReactingToNexusEvents","url":"\/documentation\/firebladeecs\/reactingtonexusevents","title":"Reacting to Nexus events","type":"topic"},"doc://FirebladeECS/documentation/FirebladeECS/MigratingToFirebladeECS2":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Move a project from FirebladeECS 1.x to 2.0: components become value types, and every write goes through the nexus."}],"role":"article","kind":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/MigratingToFirebladeECS2","url":"\/documentation\/firebladeecs\/migratingtofirebladeecs2","title":"Migrating to FirebladeECS 2","type":"topic"},"https://fireblade-engine.github.io/ecs/benchmarks/2.0.0/":{"identifier":"https:\/\/fireblade-engine.github.io\/ecs\/benchmarks\/2.0.0\/","title":"FirebladeECS 1.4.3 vs 2.0.0","url":"https:\/\/fireblade-engine.github.io\/ecs\/benchmarks\/2.0.0\/","type":"link","titleInlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"FirebladeECS 1.4.3 vs 2.0.0"}]},"doc://FirebladeECS/documentation/FirebladeECS":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A lightweight, fast and easy to use Entity-Component System in Swift."}],"role":"collection","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS","url":"\/documentation\/firebladeecs","title":"FirebladeECS","type":"topic"},"doc://FirebladeECS/documentation/FirebladeECS/Nexus/StorageKind":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The storage a "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Nexus","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" keeps its entities and components in."}],"role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"StorageK